From 2288f6f24b6900b97c7a502d959bc9c719d7a977 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:19:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 37/40] clk: qcom: gcc-kaanapali: Enable FORCE_MEM_CORE_ON for
 UFS AXI PHY clock

As on SM8650, SM8750 and Eliza, the UFS AXI PHY clock needs
FORCE_MEM_CORE_ON for the UFS controller in MCQ mode. Without it the MCQ
configuration is lost over system suspend, and with MCQ enabled every
resume from s2idle ends in an SMMU fault and a host reset.

The UFS PHY ICE core clock already has the bit set; set it for the UFS
PHY AXI clock as well.

Fixes: d1919c375f21 ("clk: qcom: Add support for Global clock controller on Kaanapali")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>

[ from patchwork.kernel.org series 1180949, patch 1; not applied upstream yet ]
[ up3: context rebased (our gcc-kaanapali.c sets the PCIe pipe clock bits after the UFS ICE line); same one-line change. ]
[ upstream author: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>; picked for the iceland kernel q89 ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c
index cdcbe54a4..e52367693 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-kaanapali.c
@@ -3484,6 +3484,7 @@ static void clk_kaanapali_regs_configure(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regm
 
 	/* FORCE_MEM_CORE_ON for ufs phy ice core clocks */
 	qcom_branch_set_force_mem_core(regmap, gcc_ufs_phy_ice_core_clk, true);
+	qcom_branch_set_force_mem_core(regmap, gcc_ufs_phy_axi_clk, true);
 
 	qcom_branch_set_force_mem_core(regmap, gcc_pcie_0_pipe_clk, true);
 	qcom_branch_set_force_periph_on(regmap, gcc_pcie_0_pipe_clk, true);
-- 
